        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Ultrasonic timing diagram"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Operation matches the earlier HC-SR04. The external MCU applies a high-level pulse longer than 10 uS to Trig; the module returns a high-level pulse proportional to distance, calculated from pulse width 'T':"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "s11",
      "heading": "Distance=T*C/2  (C is the speed of sound)",
      "level": 1,
      "page_range": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "table_count": 0,
      "table_headers_preview": [],
      "text_length_chars": 260,
      "content_keywords": [
        "330",
        "331",
        "61t",
        "45m",
        "342"
      ],
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Speed of sound versus temperature: c=(331.45+0.61t/C)m*s-1 (330.45 at 0 C)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Speed of sound at 0 C: 330.45 M/S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Speed of sound at 20 C: 342.62 M/S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Speed of sound at 40 C: 354.85 M/S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "The speed-of-sound variation from 0 C to 40 C is approximately 7%. Applications requiring precise distance values must account for temperature effects and apply temperature compensation."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "4                                                                                    WWW.WX-RCWL.COM"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Wuxi Richen IoT Technology"
        }
